9. What would happen if there is no valid solution for a given N?
•	Answer:
If there is no valid solution, the algorithm will exhaust all possible configurations and backtrack all the way to the first queen without finding a valid placement. In such cases, the algorithm will terminate, indicating that no solution exists for the given value of N.
