10. What is the time complexity of the backtracking solution for the N-Queens problem?
•	Answer:
The time complexity of the backtracking algorithm for the N-Queens problem is O(N!). This is because in the worst case, the algorithm needs to explore all possible ways to place the N queens, which is roughly N factorial (N!) possible configurations. However, backtracking helps prune the search space by eliminating invalid configurations early, which can sometimes reduce the actual time complexity.
